---The World table contains access to a variety of information about the current game world.
---@class World
World = {}

---Returns whether the world data can currently be accessed.
---@return boolean # Whether the world data is available to read from.
function World.IsAvailable() end

---Returns whether the currently connected world is a Member's world.
---@return boolean # Whether the world is a Member's world.
function World.IsMembers() end

---Returns the ping value to the current game world.
---
---This function will return `-1` if there is no active connection to a game world.
---
---Info: This function has an internal limit of 5 seconds per ping request.
---@return integer # The ping value to the current game world.
function World.GetPing() end

---Returns the number of logic ticks (50 per second) until the currently connected server reboots.
---
---Info: This will return `0` if the world is unavailable or no reboot is currently scheduled.
---@return integer # The number of logic ticks until a server reboot.
function World.GetRebootTimer() end

---Returns whether the current game world is a region or not.
---
---Info: A region is a duplicated area outside of the main game world, typically to allow players to experience content
---alone or within a group. A `Region` is often known in game-terms as an `Instance`. The term `region` is used to
---clearly differentiate this concept from other uses of `instance` in the API.
---@return boolean # Whether the current game world is a region.
function World.IsRegion() end

---Returns the source coordinate for a given region CoordGrid.
---
---Info: Regions are constructed by referencing data from other parts of the game world. Referenced zones (8x8 tiles)
---and map squares (64x64 tiles) are copied into the target region to populate it. The input CoordGrid is used to find
---the source data which that coordinate was populated from. Once the source data is found, this method returns its
---bottom-left CoordGrid.
---@param coord CoordGrid The input coordinate.
---@return CoordGrid? # The bottom-left CoordGrid for the input coordinate's source data. Returns `nil` if the Player Character is not currently in a region, or the input coordinate was outside of the region bounds.
function World.GetRegionSourceForCoordGrid(coord) end

---Returns the map square bounds for the currently loaded game world.
---
---Info: Values are in numbers of map squares. For example, when in a Dungeoneering region/instance this function
---returns:
---@return Rect? # The rectangle encompassing the current World's map square bounds.
function World.GetMapSquareBounds() end

---Returns the height for the given level and position values, along with whether the height was available for that
---position.
---
---All positional values are in fine units, where a tile dimension is `512` fine units.
---
---Info: Valid height values are always positive. A value of `-1` will be returned if the height could not be accessed.
---@param level integer The coordinate level of height map data to read. The value of `level` must be between `0` and `3`.
---@param x integer The world-space X position, in fine units, to access the height value for.
---@param z integer The world-space Z position, in fine units, to access the height value for.
---@param heightOffsetType? HeightOffsetType
---@return integer # The height and success pair for the input position values. Returns a height of `-1` on failure.
---@return boolean
function World.GetGroundHeight(level, x, z, heightOffsetType) end

---The Remove Roof system allows the client to hide upper levels of the game world in order to provide a clearer view to
---players. Portions of the game world, such as the upper floors of a building, are grouped together and hidden as a
---whole when the system is told to 'reveal' a coordinate on a level underneath the group.
---
---Some coordinates are marked in this way by default, such as:
---
---The functions below allow plugins to add individual coordinates, and coordinate ranges, to further extend which parts
---of the game world should be hidden by this system.
---
---Warning: These functions will only impact the Remove Roof system if the `Graphics` setting for `Remove Roofs` is set
---to `Selectively`.
---@class World.RemoveRoof
World.RemoveRoof = {}

---Adds the given coordinate to the Remove Roof system, registering it by the given name.
---
---If the name has already been registered then the existing coordinate, or coordinate range, is updated with the new
---coordinate.
---@param name string The name to register the coordinate with.
---@param coord CoordGrid The coordinate to add to the Remove Roof system.
---@overload fun(name: string, coordRangeMin: CoordGrid, coordRangeMax: CoordGrid)
function World.RemoveRoof.Add(name, coord) end

---Removes the coordinate, or coordinate range, registered by the given name from the Remove Roof system.
---@param name string The registered name to remove.
function World.RemoveRoof.Remove(name) end

---Removes all Remove Roof coordinates registered by the current plugin.
function World.RemoveRoof.Clear() end

---Used with World.GetGroundHeight() to apply additional offsets to the ground height, depending on the type of
---LocEntity placed at the sampled position.
---@enum HeightOffsetType
HeightOffsetType = {
    ---Applies no offset to the ground height
    NONE = 0,
    ---Applies any offset from a LocEntity using LocShapeType.GROUNDDECOR, i.e. a rug. See LocType.groundDecorOffset.
    GROUND_DECOR = 1,
    ---Offsets the height by the total height of the LocEntity, i.e. a table.
    LOCATION = 2,
}
